{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And you shall have a peg for your ear</b> a hint that if one hears foul speech he should bend his finger into his ear, and this is 'you shall go outside' — not to hear foul speech, go outside the house or bend your finger into your ear. And in the Midrash: 'and a peg' — upon the merit of the fathers, which is like a driven peg for Israel. ויתד in gematria: והאבות." "<b>and a peg shall be</b> for you upon your ear. In gematria: מדותי תהיה על אזנך. That is, the Thirteen Attributes shall be your weapon." "<b>And you shall dig</b> — two times in the Masorah; the other (Job 11:18) וחפרת לבטח תשכב. This is what they said: a person should always examine himself for his needs before sleeping — 'and you shall dig and cover your excrement,' and then 'וחפרת לבטח תשכב' (and you shall dig, you shall lie down secure)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:28.120583332Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}